argue:
A prisoner sits, engirt by secret doors
And waving tapestries that argue forth
Strange passages into the outer air;

argyin:
De times is mighty stirrin' 'mong de people up ouah way,
Dey 'sputin' an' dey argyin' an' fussin' night an' day;
An' all dis monst'ous trouble dat hit meks me tiahed to tell

argent:
But I was safe for that time, and he too;
The argent angels in the altar-flare
Absorbed his soul, next moment. The good man!

argives:
and left me free,
free to desert the Argives,
let them burn,

argile:
Comme l'amour, comme la mort;
Et j'ai fait les plus belles de belle argile
Sèche et fragile.
